## What happened

The [archived incident narrative](https://github.com/0zminDev/mega-s01-e03/blob/main/support-kb/4471-original.svx)
says one known parser issue and one queued fix.
Its rendered components disagree: the merged reports include a separate booking-form hint
problem without a ticket of its own. The old [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) is stale, and
its own explorer contradicts its subject-only rule.

This postmortem uses the **2026-10-04 export** for report counts and the subsequent course
engineering update for closure. The desk continued working while the review ran. Refreshing
the export returned identical data, so it remains a historical snapshot, not a live view.

## Current disposition: course engineering update

After the course accepted the two tickets, its
[challenge page](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) published this update:

> #4471 · closed 05 oct
>
> parser — FIXED — fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales
>
