[Issue 1](https://github.com/0zminDev/mega-s01-e03/issues/1) is closed as **completed** on the
desk's report of the parser fix.
[Issue 2](https://github.com/0zminDev/mega-s01-e03/issues/2) is closed as **not planned** because the
affected form was retired, not because its hint was repaired. These dispositions come from
the current course update; the export below still describes the earlier state.

The update does not establish that each of the flagged one-day/chronology reports was
reproduced or fixed. Preserve those uncertainties instead of claiming verification we do not have.

## Problems and tickets

- [Parser problem: GitHub issue 1](https://github.com/0zminDev/mega-s01-e03/issues/1).
  The shared parser assumed month first for day-first tenants. Engineering reports that
  day-first parsing was fixed.
- [Form hint problem: GitHub issue 2](https://github.com/0zminDev/mega-s01-e03/issues/2).
  For day-first tenants on booking-v3, the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` but reads the tenant's
  day-first order. Engineering retired that form rather than repairing its hint.
  A shared-parser fix alone does not repair this form contract.

The following table computes the reports covered by each problem from unique report IDs.
Its final column describes the **original desk ticket**, not the new GitHub issues above.
Do not use the intake tags as the cause: they are guesses based on the reporter's browser.
Resolve the report's tenant locale and booking-form version instead.

